ssed through the application of emerging technologies, and then develop a practical solution to that challenge.\n\n**Scope:** The scope of this project includes researching and selecting a suitable problem statement, designing and developing a solution, testing and validating the solution, and finally deploying and maintaining the system.\n\n**Expected Outcome:** The expected outcome of this project is a fully functional system that demonstrates the team's ability to work together to design, develop, and deploy an innovative solution to a real-world problem.\n\n## 2. Measurable Objectives\n\n1. To research and select a suitable problem statement that aligns with the team's skills and interests\n2. To design and develop a solution that integrates multiple technologies such as AI, machine learning, cloud computing, and IoT\n3. To test and validate the solution to ensure it meets the required specifications and is free from defects\n4. To deploy and maintain the system, and provide ongoing support and updates as needed\n\n## 3. Project Deliverables\n\n- A written report detailing the problem statement, solution design, and development process\n- A fully functional system that demonstrates the team's ability to design, develop, and deploy an innovative solution\n- A presentation that showcases the system's features and capabilities\n- A maintenance and support plan that outlines the team's approach to ensuring the system remains operational and up-to-date\n\n## 4. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\n\n| ID | Package Name | Percentage | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `pkg-1` | Problem Statement Research and Selection | 15% | Research and select a suitable problem statement that aligns with the team's skills and interests |\n| `pkg-2` | Solution Design and Development | 40% | Design and develop a solution that integrates multiple technologies such as AI, machine learning, cloud computing, and IoT |\n| `pkg-3` | Testing and Validation | 20% | Test and validate the solution to ensure it meets the required specifications and is free from defects |\n| `pkg-4` | Project Management | 10% | Manage the project timeline, resources, and budget to ensure successful completion |\n| `pkg-5` | Documentation and IPR | 15% | Create and maintain detailed documentation of the system, and ensure that all intellectual property rights are protected |\n\n## 5. Required Skills\n\n- Big Data Analytics and machine learning\n- Cloud Computing\n- DevOps and IT Infra\n- Generative AI (Gen AI)\n- Natural Language Processing\n- Prompt Engineering\n- Cyber Security and Cryptography\n- Full-Stack Software Development\n- IoT and Sensor Integration\n- User Experience (UI/UX) Design\n\n## 6. Milestones & Schedule\n\n| Milestone | Expected Output | Completion Week |\n|---|---|---|\n| Problem Statement Selected | A written report detailing the selected problem statement | Week 4 |\n| Solution Design Completed | A detailed design document outlining the solution architecture | Week 8 |\n| Solution Development Completed | A fully functional system that demonstrates the team's ability to design, develop, and deploy an innovative solution | Week 16 |\n| Testing and Validation Completed | A written report detailing the testing and validation results | Week 20 |\n\n## 7. Risk Management\n\n- Delays in selecting a suitable problem statement\n- Technical difficulties in developing the solution\n- Insufficient resources or budget to complete the project\n- Changes in team members or their availability\n\n## 8. Learning Resources\n\n- **AI and Machine Learning:** Online courses and tutorials on AI and machine learning ([Link](https://www.coursera.org/))\n- **Cloud Computing:** Online courses and tutorials on cloud computing ([Link](https://aws.amazon.com/))\n- **IoT and Sensor Integration:** Online courses and tutorials on IoT and sensor integration ([Link](https://www.edx.org/))\n\n## 9. Success Criteria\n\n- The system is fully functional and meets the required specifications\n- The system is free from defects and performs as expected\n- The system is deployed and maintained successfully\n- The team demonstrates good project management and communication skills\n\n	2026-07-27 05:33:55.363
