 {"topic": "TensorFlow", "resource": "Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for TensorFlow"}, {"topic": "PostgreSQL", "resource": "Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for PostgreSQL"}, {"topic": "FastAPI", "resource": "Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for FastAPI"}]}	# Execution Document: Using existing CCTV network for crowd management\n\n> **Uniqueness & Scope Variation Notes:**\n> The project's uniqueness lies in its ability to leverage the existing CCTV network for crowd management, providing a cost-effective and efficient solution for public safety and security.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\n**Background:** The existing CCTV network can be leveraged for crowd management by utilizing computer vision and machine learning techniques to analyze footage and provide insights on crowd density, movement, and behavior.\n\n**Purpose:** To develop a system that utilizes the existing CCTV network for effective crowd management, enhancing public safety and security.\n\n**Problem Statement:** The lack of an efficient crowd management system can lead to safety risks, congestion, and decreased quality of experience in public spaces.\n\n**Scope:** The project aims to design, develop, and deploy a crowd management system using the existing CCTV network, focusing on a specific geographic area or event.\n\n**Expected Outcome:** A functional crowd management system that provides real-time insights and alerts, enabling authorities to take proactive measures to ensure public safety and security.\n\n## 2. Measurable Objectives\n\n1. To design and develop a computer vision-based system for crowd density analysis\n2. To integrate the system with the existing CCTV network\n3. To develop a machine learning model for predicting crowd behavior and detecting anomalies\n4. To create a user-friendly interface for authorities to monitor and respond to crowd-related events\n\n## 3. Project Deliverables\n\n- A fully functional crowd management system\n- A detailed report on the system's design, development, and testing\n- A user manual for the system\n- A presentation summarizing the project's outcomes and impact\n\n## 4. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\n\n| ID | Package Name | Percentage | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `pkg-1` | System Design and Development | 40% | Design and develop the computer vision and machine learning components of the system |\n| `pkg-2` | Integration with CCTV Network | 20% | Integrate the system with the existing CCTV network |\n| `pkg-3` | Testing and Validation | 20% | Test and validate the system's performance and accuracy |\n| `pkg-4` | Project Management | 10% | Manage the project timeline, resources, and team |\n| `pkg-5` | Documentation/IPR | 10% | Document the system's design, development, and testing, and ensure intellectual property rights are protected |\n\n## 5. Required Skills\n\n- Computer Vision\n- Machine Learning\n- Python\n- TensorFlow\n- PostgreSQL\n- FastAPI\n- Full-Stack Software Development\n\n## 6. Milestones & Schedule\n\n| Milestone | Expected Output | Completion Week |\n|---|---|---|\n| System Design Completion | A detailed system design document | Week 4 |\n| System Development Completion | A fully functional system | Week 12 |\n| Integration with CCTV Network Completion | A fully integrated system | Week 16 |\n| Testing and Validation Completion | A fully tested and validated system | Week 20 |\n\n## 7. Risk Management\n\n- Delays in system development\n- Inaccurate crowd density analysis\n- Integration issues with CCTV network\n- Insufficient testing and validation\n\n## 8. Learning Resources\n\n- **Computer Vision:** OpenCV documentation and tutorials ([Link](https://docs.opencv.org/))\n- **Machine Learning:** TensorFlow documentation and tutorials ([Link](https://www.tensorflow.org/))\n- **Python:** Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for Python\n- **TensorFlow:** Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for TensorFlow\n- **PostgreSQL:** Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for PostgreSQL\n- **FastAPI:** Search official documentation, freeCodeCamp, or NPTEL tutorials for FastAPI\n\n## 9. Success Criteria\n\n- The system accurately analyzes crowd density and detects anomalies\n- The system is fully integrated with the existing CCTV network\n- The system provides real-time insights and alerts to authorities\n- The system is user-friendly and easy to maintain\n\n	2026-07-27 05:54:24.447
